267 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 542 0 R
/E (The analysis was based on a data of a small sample size \(n = 8\), whose design was fairly balanced, with no extreme library sizes or compositional biases; this may be why simple scaling already performs well. Robinson & Oshlack \(2010\) show that TMM is particularly helpful when a small subset of genes changes dramatically or when libraries differ strongly in composition. )
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
268 0 obj
<<
